@ [exploded] C:\Project\Cantor\specifications\exploded\Cantor_Recursive_Machine_Schema_Profile.exploded.sop

& [Representation] is finite local reference graph
  + ProcedureType and ProcedureValue each have one stable named definition
  + recursive members reference their named definition through fragment-local Draft 2020-12 references
  + canonical documents contain no external, file, relative-document, network, or dynamically retrieved reference
  + recursive references are not dereferenced during normalization or digesting

& [GraphClosure] is deterministic
  + every local reference target exists in the same canonical document or declared in-memory bundle
  + definition identities and traversal order use stable lexical type names
  + visited identities prevent repeated expansion
  + active-path identities classify direct and mutual cycles
  + unexpected mutual cycles are refused in profile 0.1 unless explicitly listed by a later revision
  + known direct self cycles are ProcedureType and ProcedureValue only

& [ResourceAccounting] includes cycles
  + each named definition counts once
  + each reference occurrence counts once even when its target is already visited
  + document depth counts schema syntax without following references
  + definition graph depth ends a path at a visited target
  + all CPMS profile 0.1 byte, definition, reference, property, alternative, residual, and corpus ceilings remain active

& [InstanceDepth] is layered
  + JSON parsing retains the active serde_json container recursion limit and never disables it
  + schema validation uses only an in-memory registry and a separately bounded instance traversal
  + Cantor validates ProcedureBounds.maximum_call_depth as positive and no greater than 64
  + Cantor recursively validates ProcedureType and ProcedureValue by decrementing maximum_call_depth
  + value byte, text, collection, and map bounds remain semantic residuals
  + enclosing transport objects may cause serde to reject before the semantic depth ceiling and that distinction is explicit

& [Conformance] is boundary aware
  + schema meta-validation must accept the canonical recursive documents
  + schema validation and strict serde must agree on every claimed expressible syntax rule
  + depth limits not expressible in Draft 2020-12 remain named residuals
  + safe complete fixtures exercise shallow recursion, every recursive variant, semantic boundary values, parser-depth boundary values, unresolved targets, external references, and cycle counter exhaustion
  + no disagreement, panic, stack overflow, network attempt, or partial schema escapes as success

& [Compatibility] preserves public forms
  + no finite unrolling
  + no alternate transport projection
  + no change to ProcedureType, ProcedureValue, prepare, run, verify, response, or CLI bytes
  + recursive schema support is additive to the canonical derivation layer only

& [ImplementationSequence] is narrow
  + RMS-I01 add exact recursive JsonSchema derivation and stable local names under the separately authorized CPMS-I02 slice
  + RMS-I02 implement cycle-safe closure validation, normalization, counters, and typed faults
  + RMS-I03 add recursive boundary conformance cases and residual registry bindings
  + each step requires focused review before the next

& [AuthorityBoundary] is formation only
  + this specification resolves the representation decision but does not activate implementation
  - never: add a dependency, generate a schema, alter public transport, disable parser limits, retrieve a reference, register a provider tool, call a model, use a service, persist, network, effect, or hardware

& [SignatureCandidate] is formed not activated
  + [candidate_signature_uuid] is cdf5a4fe-6f57-4b06-b304-7c8657a9528f
  + [activation_condition] is exact canonical hash, schema-library pin, source-type derive blast-radius review, and CPMS-I02 claim

